Build 030A, instrumentation only (GPT's 029 review, handoff2.md section 5): nothing changes in rendering.
- readers.txt binds are recorded after the feedback substitution (ReplaceColorFeedbackViews) and carry
  the image's and the view's pixel formats and whether the feedback copy was bound instead.
- With /data/eden-nx2/capture-watch.txt (EDEN_NX2_CAPTURE_WATCH, guest addresses) a capture also writes
  sequence.txt: the armed frame's draws and dispatches that bind or render to a watched image, in order,
  with render target 0 and its format. And stages/: up to 12 snapshots of the watched image before each
  draw that touches it and after each draw or dispatch that touches it (pre-fog, post-fog, post-pack).
  Snapshots are only taken at a draw, so the GPU wait never falls inside a compute dispatch.

